# Two males frustrated at once - bar contention (undocumented behavior)
# What happens when both males become frustrated close together. hardware/bar/__init__.py's loop() only checks "is any male searching" - it has no concept of "which male", so this timeline traces the actual, somewhat arbitrary resulting behavior rather than an intended design. See SCENARIOS.md 7.2.

0 male1's O drive crosses the frustration threshold (75); male1.search starts (sway + blink male1's "O" pattern)
0 bar.loop() sees male1 searching and starts bar.search: full-range wander begins
40 ~ bar wanders full-range while only male1 is frustrated
0 male2's P drive also crosses the frustration threshold; male2.search starts too (sway + blink male2's own "P" pattern, independently of male1's)
0 bar.loop() re-checks "is any male searching" every tick - already True, so nothing about the bar's own search changes; it keeps wandering the same full range it already was, now serving neither male's specific interaction origin more than the other
60 ~ both males sway and blink simultaneously (different patterns, different physical positions) while the single shared bar wanders past whichever (male, female) interaction origin it happens to be near - nothing biases the bar toward the more-frustrated or earlier-frustrated male
0 If a female becomes unsatisfied during this window, her read_pattern only decodes a match if the bar happens to be at the right interaction origin AND the right male's ring is lit at the right instant - with two males both blinking, near-simultaneous alignment becomes plausible but is not coordinated by any code
0 Neither male's search nor the bar's search has a stop condition tied to satisfaction (SCENARIOS.md 1.2/4.1) - both keep running until something external stops them or a drive is otherwise reset
